2026/10/13 09:31:54 [DEBUG] Z.AI SSE line: data: {"type":"chat:completion","data":{"delta_content":"[ref_id=turn2fetch0†What's New in Oracle AI? October 2026 Edition†https://blogs.oracle.com/ai-and-datascience/whats-new-in-oracle-ai-october-2026]\n**viewing lines [1-67] of 160**\nL1: * 【0†Accessibility Policy】\nL2: 【1†Oracle】\nL3: 【2†Oracle AI & Data Science Blog】\nL4: Search\nL5: Exit Search Field\nL6: Clear Search Field\nL7: Menu\nL8: CATEGORIES* 【3†AI in Business】\nL9: * 【4†Best Practices】\nL10: * 【5†Learn Data Science】\nL11: * 【6†NetSuite SDN】\nL12: * 【7†Oracle Analytics Cloud & Server】\nL13: * 【8†Oracle Certification】\nL14: * 【9†Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI)】\nL15: * 【10†Partner Solutions】\nL16: * 【11†Product News】\nL17: * 【12†Technical Solutions】\nL18: * 【13†Training and Upskilling】\nL19: * 【14†Use Cases】\nL20: * 【15†Oracle AI】【16†Back】\nL21: + 【17†Oracle AI】\nL22: + 【18†Oracle Labs】\nL23: * 【19†Blogs Home】\nL24: * 【20†RSS】\nL25: Oracle AI & Data Science Blog\nL26: Follow:\nL27: * 【21†RSS】\nL28: * Facebook\nL29: * Twitter\nL30: * LinkedIn\nL31: * YouTube\nL32: * Instagram\nL33: 【22†Facebook】\nL34: 【23†Twitter】\nL35: 【24†LinkedIn】\nL36: 【25†Email】\nL37: 【26†Oracle AI】, 【27†Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI)】, 【28†Product News】\nL38: # What’s New in Oracle AI? October 2026 Edition\nL39: October 9, 2026\nL40: 5 minute read\nL41: 【29†Michelle Meng】Product Marketing Director\nL42: Oracle AI World is right around the corner, and we’re gearing up for a big October. Before we head to Las Vegas, catch up on the latest OCI Enterprise AI updates from last month, including new Grok models, Smart Model Router, model discovery, and expanded Model Import options. Then, get ready for AI World with our recommended sessions and a hands-on hackathon where you can put OCI AI capabilities to work.\nL43: ### **New updates and features:**\nL44: **xAI Grok 4.6 and Grok 4.7 now available in OCI Enterprise AI**\nL45: xAI Grok 4.6 and Grok 4.7 are now available for on-demand inference in OCI Enterprise AI. The models are designed for coding, agentic tasks, reasoning, and knowledge work, giving customers access to xAI’s latest capabilities without having to manage the underlying infrastructure.\nL46: These additions give organizations more choice when matching models to complex workloads and make it easier to evaluate the latest xAI models alongside other models available in OCI Enterprise AI.\nL47: 【30†Learn more about】**【31†Grok】**【32†4.6】 and 【33†Grok 4.7】\nL48: **Smart model router simplifies cross-region AI inference**\nL49: OCI Enterprise AI now offers Smart Model Router, which routes on-demand inference requests across customer-selected OCI regions where a model is available. Customers create a routing profile that defines the model and approved regions, then use that profile with the Chat API or Responses API.\nL50: For customers running AI applications at scale, this can help applications access available model capacity across approved regions without requiring teams to build and maintain their own cross-region routing logic. Customers remain in control of the regional scope in which inference can occur.\nL51: 【34†Learn more: Smart Model Router】\nL52: **Model discovery makes it easier to find the right model**\nL53: OCI Enterprise AI now supports Model Discovery, giving developers API access to discover models available in a specific region and retrieve details such as capabilities, input and output types, serving options, supported parameters, and retirement dates. Instead of relying on manually maintained model lists or configurations, developers can programmatically discover available models and use that information when building applications, making it easier to adapt as new models and capabilities become available.\nL54: 【35†Learn more: Model Discovery】\nL55: **More models available through Model Import**\nL56: OCI Enterprise AI continued to expand Model Import in September, adding support for models from Alibaba, DeepSeek, Google, and Z.ai. New additions include:\nL57: * Alibaba Qwen3.8-27B and Qwen3.5-397B-A17B\nL58: * DeepSeek V4 Pro 0813 and DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\nL59: * Google Gemma 4 31B IT and Gemma 4 26B A4B IT\nL60: * Z.ai GLM-5.3 and GLM-5.3-Flash\nL61: The expanding catalog gives customers more options for choosing models based on the capabilities, performance, and economics required by each workload, rather than taking a one-size-fits-all approach to model selection.\nL62: 【36†Explore models available for import: Models for Import】\nL63: **OCI Responses API adds support for imported models**\nL64: The OCI Responses API can now call select models deployed through Model Import, beginning with Alibaba Qwen3.6-35B-A3B and Google Gemma 4 31B IT. Customers first import and host the model on a compatible dedicated AI cluster and can then access it through the Responses API.\nL65: This gives developers a more consistent API experience across OCI Enterprise AI model options and makes it easier to incorporate imported models into applications that already use the Responses API.\nL66: 【37†Learn more: ⁠Imported models with the OCI Responses API】\nL67: **More granular model access controls with OCI IAM**","phase":"tool_response","tool_name":"open","status":"completed","metadata":{"browser":{"refid":"turn2fetch0","url":"https://blogs.oracle.com/ai-and-datascience/whats-new-in-oracle-ai-october-2026","title":"What's New in Oracle AI? October 2026 Edition","content":"[ref_id=turn2fetch0†What's New in Oracle AI? October 2026 Edition†https://blogs.oracle.com/ai-and-datascience/whats-new-in-oracle-ai-october-2026]\n**viewing lines [1-67] of 160**\nL1: * 【0†Accessibility Policy】\nL2: 【1†Oracle】\nL3: 【2†Oracle AI & Data Science Blog】\nL4: Search\nL5: Exit Search Field\nL6: Clear Search Field\nL7: Menu\nL8: CATEGORIES* 【3†AI in Business】\nL9: * 【4†Best Practices】\nL10: * 【5†Learn Data Science】\nL11: * 【6†NetSuite SDN】\nL12: * 【7†Oracle Analytics Cloud & Server】\nL13: * 【8†Oracle Certification】\nL14: * 【9†Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI)】\nL15: * 【10†Partner Solutions】\nL16: * 【11†Product News】\nL17: * 【12†Technical Solutions】\nL18: * 【13†Training and Upskilling】\nL19: * 【14†Use Cases】\nL20: * 【15†Oracle AI】【16†Back】\nL21: + 【17†Oracle AI】\nL22: + 【18†Oracle Labs】\nL23: * 【19†Blogs Home】\nL24: * 【20†RSS】\nL25: Oracle AI & Data Science Blog\nL26: Follow:\nL27: * 【21†RSS】\nL28: * Facebook\nL29: * Twitter\nL30: * LinkedIn\nL31: * YouTube\nL32: * Instagram\nL33: 【22†Facebook】\nL34: 【23†Twitter】\nL35: 【24†LinkedIn】\nL36: 【25†Email】\nL37: 【26†Oracle AI】, 【27†Oracle Cloud Infrastructure (OCI)】, 【28†Product News】\nL38: # What’s New in Oracle AI? October 2026 Edition\nL39: October 9, 2026\nL40: 5 minute read\nL41: 【29†Michelle Meng】Product Marketing Director\nL42: Oracle AI World is right around the corner, and we’re gearing up for a big October. Before we head to Las Vegas, catch up on the latest OCI Enterprise AI updates from last month, including new Grok models, Smart Model Router, model discovery, and expanded Model Import options. Then, get ready for AI World with our recommended sessions and a hands-on hackathon where you can put OCI AI capabilities to work.\nL43: ### **New updates and features:**\nL44: **xAI Grok 4.6 and Grok 4.7 now available in OCI Enterprise AI**\nL45: xAI Grok 4.6 and Grok 4.7 are now available for on-demand inference in OCI Enterprise AI. The models are designed for coding, agentic tasks, reasoning, and knowledge work, giving customers access to xAI’s latest capabilities without having to manage the underlying infrastructure.\nL46: These additions give organizations more choice when matching models to complex workloads and make it easier to evaluate the latest xAI models alongside other models available in OCI Enterprise AI.\nL47: 【30†Learn more about】**【31†Grok】**【32†4.6】 and 【33†Grok 4.7】\nL48: **Smart model router simplifies cross-region AI inference**\nL49: OCI Enterprise AI now offers Smart Model Router, which routes on-demand inference requests across customer-selected OCI regions where a model is available. Customers create a routing profile that defines the model and approved regions, then use that profile with the Chat API or Responses API.\nL50: For customers running AI applications at scale, this can help applications access available model capacity across approved regions without requiring teams to build and maintain their own cross-region routing logic. Customers remain in control of the regional scope in which inference can occur.\nL51: 【34†Learn more: Smart Model Router】\nL52: **Model discovery makes it easier to find the right model**\nL53: OCI Enterprise AI now supports Model Discovery, giving developers API access to discover models available in a specific region and retrieve details such as capabilities, input and output types, serving options, supported parameters, and retirement dates. Instead of relying on manually maintained model lists or configurations, developers can programmatically discover available models and use that information when building applications, making it easier to adapt as new models and capabilities become available.\nL54: 【35†Learn more: Model Discovery】\nL55: **More models available through Model Import**\nL56: OCI Enterprise AI continued to expand Model Import in September, adding support for models from Alibaba, DeepSeek, Google, and Z.ai. New additions include:\nL57: * Alibaba Qwen3.8-27B and Qwen3.5-397B-A17B\nL58: * DeepSeek V4 Pro 0813 and DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\nL59: * Google Gemma 4 31B IT and Gemma 4 26B A4B IT\nL60: * Z.ai GLM-5.3 and GLM-5.3-Flash\nL61: The expanding catalog gives customers more options for choosing models based on the capabilities, performance, and economics required by each workload, rather than taking a one-size-fits-all approach to model selection.\nL62: 【36†Explore models available for import: Models for Import】\nL63: **OCI Responses API adds support for imported models**\nL64: The OCI Responses API can now call select models deployed through Model Import, beginning with Alibaba Qwen3.6-35B-A3B and Google Gemma 4 31B IT. Customers first import and host the model on a compatible dedicated AI cluster and can then access it through the Responses API.\nL65: This gives developers a more consistent API experience across OCI Enterprise AI model options and makes it easier to incorporate imported models into applications that already use the Responses API.\nL66: 【37†Learn more: ⁠Imported models with the OCI Responses API】\nL67: **More granular model access controls with OCI IAM**","session_id":"7e2588f5-a266-4cd3-9e8b-a89ca199ea7f","turn_count":3},"tool_call_id":"call_8c94d5737bc948a5881b8368"}}}
