, path: str) — Write UTF-8 text to a writable Agent workspace file. mode replace writes the com...\n- workspace_apply_patch(new_string: str, old_string: str, path: str, replace_all?: bool) — Apply a precise single-file string replacement. old_string must come from text y...\n- workspace_shell(command: str, workdir?: str) — Run workspace commands for scripts, pipelines, data processing, batch changes, a...\n- workspace_commit(mode?: str, path?: str, reason?: str) — Commit a workspace text file to this run's single chat message. With no argument...\n- workspace_finish(reason?: str) — Finish the Agent run after required chat commits and workspace changes are compl...\n\nInput: \"Ok so let's take things step by step and not get too hasty and starting to jump to generate workout plans but instead they should be carefully measured and intelegntly set and crafted for the best (don't construct any plan untill i tell you focus on the other things). So first i don't want like traditional training or like generic stuff, my ambitions are above the stars so conventional training won't do it. So first we need you to assess me so you have concrete data you can build on. I've found these two videos that i think are extremely necessary for reaching my goal: https://youtu.be/2-7QZVEjW9U?si=8n_kUWZrQt7TBgO0\nhttps://youtu.be/70i14YxUTbc?si=v2gXWvhVCDX4XGR6 \nThey explain a approach that makes sense and actually feel like it directly feed my ambitions (more details in what the vids explain ofc) \nAlso i think one of the most necessary things are for discipline and never stopping is missions or something a bit \"gamefied\". Also I want to be able to kill people according to superhuman assassin goal and know how to use stuff not only boxing or grappling.\nAnd for your questions:\nSo in my garden there's a lot of things more than i count, there's a lot of things that can be used in different ways there are tree branches, thick bar (i cant close my hand around it), heavy metal bar that i usually used to swing (like mace exercises) it or throw it like a spear, I've got rubber bands different sizes, I've got walls big and small also walls with holes in them, I've got a chain... etc there's things that i may have forgot to mention but pretty much there's a lot of freedom. 2 my budget isn't really high but i can try to manage 3 sadly no, i just faintly remeber that there's a small parkour club and there's also mma and wrestling but it's in a different state that's almost 2 hours away and they usually train at night and i can't go home in time (also family issues).\"","models":["glm-5.3"]}},"currentId":"7c200965-0467-4d72-ab24-e64aa2673e3a"},"tags":[],"features":[{"type":"tool_selector","server":"tool_selector_h","status":"hidden"}],"mcp_servers":["advanced-search"],"enable_thinking":true,"reasoning_effort":"max","auto_web_search":true,"timestamp":1791909407085,"extra":{}},"updated_at":1791909407,"created_at":1791909407,"share_id":null,"archived":false,"pinned":false,"meta":{"auto_web_search":true,"flags":null,"mcp_servers":["advanced-search"],"models":["glm-5.3"],"workspace_id":"aec9f96f-8727-45c6-928b-d54defaa79a3"},"folder_id":null,"message_version":1,"type":"default","im_context":null}
