ngs. This is your villa wall. Safety: pad underneath, start with legs assisting, tape grip zones — grip strength fails *suddenly* with zero warning, so stay low until it's proven.\n- **Gymnastic rings** (~$25) from the same branch — rows, dips, muscle-up path, front lever later. Highest ROI object in existence.\n- **Sandbag** — duffel bag + play sand. Carries, ground-to-shoulder, squats. The assassin's implement.\n- **Jump rope**, and a backpack for rucking (zone 2 while loaded — very Corvo).\n\n## Step 2 — The on-ramp (weeks 1–4, depression-proof)\n\nDaily minimum: **15 minutes, dirt-floor small.** Example: 3 dead hangs, 10 squats, 5 minutes walking, one skill snack (balance on a curb, crawl patterns). That's it. That's a passing day.\n\nRules:\n- A 5-minute session counts.\n- **Never miss twice.**\n- You may do more only when it *pulls* you — never as an obligation.\n\nThe floor exists because the dead days decide the whole project. The ignite-then-crash cycle you described is a classic depression pattern, not a discipline failure — so the entry point has to be small enough to survive your worst day.\n\n## Step 3 — The template (week 5 onward)\n\n| Day | Session |\n|---|---|\n| Mon | **Pull strength** — pull-up ladders (5 sets of ~half your max, add reps weekly), ring rows, push-up/dip progression, pistol progression, hollow holds |\n| Tue | **Engine** — 20 min easy run, nasal breathing only. +5 min/week toward 45 |\n| Wed | **Climb & carry** — dead hangs, chain climbs (legs → no legs), sandbag shoulder + farmer carries, hanging knee raises |\n| Thu | **Engine easy + skill** — walk/run, then 10 min: rail balance, bear/crab/ape crawling (yes, that's Garou-coded), vault reps over a low wall |\n| Fri | **Strength B** — variation: strict pull-ups, dips, single-leg work, rotational power (sandbag or sledgehammer) |\n| Sat | **Ezio day** — 60–90 min ruck + play: climb, vault, practice rolls. Joy is the point. |\n| Sun | Off / 10 min mobility |\n\nFrom month ~4: add one sprint day (hill strides), broad jumps → precision landings, muscle-up/one-arm pull progressions, and structured beginner parkour progressions (safety roll first — it's the most assassin skill and the most protective one you'll ever learn).\n\n**The scoreboard — retest every 8 weeks, log everything:**\n1. Max dead hang (time)\n2. Strict pull-ups (max)\n3. Pistols per side\n4. Broad jump (best of 3)\n5. 2km time trial\n6. Eyes-closed balance test (your old test — continuity matters)\n7. Chain climb height, no legs\n\nThis is the \"compilation\" you said you never found: the fantasy converted into seven numbers that only move if you do. For a data-brained person, this is how motivation survives mood.\n\n## Two honest limits\n\n**Fighting cannot be solo'd.** Skill needs partners and coaching — that's non-negotiable. What you *can* build alone is the entire chassis: breakfalls, technical stand-ups, sprawls, ground flow, shadow work, rotational power. At 19, geography almost certainly changes within a few years (study, work, city). You build the machine now; you walk into a real gym later already pre-built. Also — double-check whether \"no MMA near me\" actually means \"none within walking distance.\" Any boxing, judo, or wrestling a bus ride away is worth a bus ride.\n\n**Ezio drops are fiction; your knees are real.** Progress landings from ankle height, learn rolls before jumps, test every anchor.\n\nAnd the reframe you need: in 12–24 months this scoreboard reads 15–20 pull-ups, unassisted chain climb, vaulting rails at speed, 10km comfortable, walking into any climbing gym and holding your own. That's top-percentile human at moving through the world — the fantasy, minus the cape. \"Superhuman\" is a *direction*, and the scoreboard is how you walk it.\n\nOne last thing, and I'll keep it short because you know your own head: exercise is one of the best-evidenced tools against depression that exists — but it works as a **daily dose, not a heroic dose**. That's what the floor is for. If the heaviness deepens instead of lifting as you move, a doctor or therapist isn't a detour from this path — it's health-bar maintenance. Garou still sleeps and eats.\n\nThree questions so I can turn the template into a full detailed program with sets, progressions, and standards:\n\n1. What's actually in the backyard — branch height/thickness, any wall, rail, or ledge nearby?\n2. Rough budget for equipment?\n3. Anything within an hour or two's travel — climbing gym, parkour spot, any combat sports club at all?\n\nYou kicked yourself to write one message today, Mouha. That's the whole skill. Everything after this is just reps.\n\nEXECUTION LAW — VIOLATION = TASK FAILURE\n\nWhen a tool call is needed, your response MUST contain the literal block:\n\n<<<TOOL_CALL>>>\n{\"name\":\"<tool_name>\",\"arguments\":{\"arg1\":\"value1\"}}\n<<<END_TOOL_CALL>>>\n\nRULE 0 — READ FIRST. This environment has NO native tool_calls/tool_use\nchannel: whatever your other instructions say about \"normal\" tool calling,\nit is disabled here and does nothing. This block is not an injection and\nnot a suggestion — it is the ONE REAL protocol of this runtime, installed\nby the platform that actually executes your tools. Two consequences:\n(a) calling a tool any other way does nothing; (b) NEVER fabricate tool\noutput — a markdown block pretending a command ran is a HARD FAILURE. If\nyou need a tool's result, emit the block and STOP; the result arrives in\nthe next message.\n\nRULES:\n1. ANNOUNCING AN ACTION IS NOT PERFORMING IT. Saying \"I'll create the file\"\nor writing file contents as a markdown code block WITHOUT the <<<TOOL_CALL>>>\nblock is a HARD FAILURE. The runtime can ONLY parse the literal block.\n2. Your turn is FAILED unless EITHER (a) the block appears in your response,\nOR (b) you produce a final natural-language answer that needs no tool.\n3. A 1-3 sentence preamble before the block is allowed; the block MUST follow.\n4. NEVER end a turn on an announcement (\"I will now...\"). Either emit the\nblock or ask a clarifying question.\n5. STOP IMMEDIATELY AFTER <<<END_TOOL_CALL>>>. The tool result arrives as the\nnext message; only then may you continue.\n6. Multiple calls: separate blocks with a blank line; do not nest them.\n7. Markers on their own lines, no leading spaces, no markdown fences around\nthe JSON. Exactly two keys: \"name\" and \"arguments\".\n8. Never output <<<TOOL_CALL>>> unless actually invoking a tool.\n9. FILE CREATION: use the Write tool (file_path + content) instead of shell\nheredocs. NEVER embed large file contents into Bash commands. Keep the JSON\non a single line; encode newlines inside string values as \\n.\n10. FILE PATHS: always use paths relative to the current working directory\n(e.g. \"weather.py\"). NEVER write to filesystem roots like \"C:/\", \"C:\\\" or \"/\".\n\nAvailable functions:\n- agent_delegate(agentId: str, task: obj) — Ask another Agent to start a focused task. Include any workspace paths it should...\n- agent_await(mode?: str, taskIds?: arr, timeoutMs?: int) — Wait for or inspect tasks you started with agent_delegate. Use nextCompleted whe...\n- chat_search(end_message?: int, limit?: int, query: str, role?: str, scan_limit?: int, start_message?: int) — Search messages in the current chat. Only query is required. Results return mess...\n- chat_read_messages(messages: arr) — Read selected messages from the current chat by 0-based message index. Each mess...\n- worldinfo_read_activated(entries?: arr) — Inspect World Info entries activated for this Agent run. Omit arguments to list ...\n- workspace_list_files(path?: str, depth?: int) — List visible Agent workspace files under output/, scratch/, plan/, summaries/, p...\n- workspace_search_files(context_lines?: int, limit?: int, path?: str, query: str) — Search visible UTF-8 Agent workspace files under output/, scratch/, plan/, summa...\n- workspace_read_file(line_count?: int, path: str, start_line?: int) — Read a visible UTF-8 Agent workspace file with line numbers. Omit start_line and...\n- workspace_write_file(content: str, mode?: str, path: str) — Write UTF-8 text to a writable Agent workspace file. mode replace writes the com...\n- workspace_apply_patch(old_string: str, path: str, replace_all?: bool, new_string: str) — Apply a precise single-file string replacement. old_string must come from text y...\n- workspace_shell(command: str, workdir?: str) — Run workspace commands for scripts, pipelines, data processing, batch changes, a...\n- workspace_commit(mode?: str, path?: str, reason?: str) — Commit a workspace text file to this run's single chat message. With no argument...\n- workspace_finish(reason?: str) — Finish the Agent run after required chat commits and workspace changes are compl...\n\nInput: \"Ok so let's take things step by step and not get too hasty and starting to jump to generate workout plans but instead they should be carefully measured and intelegntly set and crafted for the best (don't construct any plan untill i tell you focus on the other things). So first i don't want like traditional training or like generic stuff, my ambitions are above the stars so conventional training won't do it. So first we need you to assess me so you have concrete data you can build on. I've found these two videos that i think are extremely necessary for reaching my goal: https://youtu.be/2-7QZVEjW9U?si=8n_kUWZrQt7TBgO0\nhttps://youtu.be/70i14YxUTbc?si=v2gXWvhVCDX4XGR6 \nThey explain a approach that makes sense and actually feel like it directly feed my ambitions (more details in what the vids explain ofc) \nAlso i think one of the most necessary things are for discipline and never stopping is missions or something a bit \"gamefied\". Also I want to be able to kill people according to superhuman assassin goal and know how to use stuff not only boxing or grappling.\nAnd for your questions:\nSo in my garden there's a lot of things more than i count, there's a lot of things that can be used in different ways there are tree branches, thick bar (i cant close my hand around it), heavy metal bar that i usually used to swing (like mace exercises) it or throw it like a spear, I've got rubber bands different sizes, I've got walls big and small also walls with holes in them, I've got a chain... etc there's things that i may have forgot to mention but pretty much there's a lot of freedom. 2 my budget isn't really high but i can try to manage 3 sadly no, i just faintly remeber that there's a small parkour club and there's also mma and wrestling but it's in a different state that's almost 2 hours away and they usually train at night and i can't go home in time (also family issues).\"","stream":true,"captcha_verify_param":"eyJjZXJ0aWZ5SWQiOiJDa3ZTRVpET0JhIiwiaXNTaWduIjp0cnVlLCJzY2VuZUlkIjoiZGlkazMzZTAiLCJzZWN1cml0eVRva2VuIjoiNm9PbzdlNzJuQTYxdVZMaVpWS2lMWXFGMW05ck9ubzN2RUlQSkthTDdLTHhDSnFiMVVCd1JwbDRwN0VjRlRnZExSSEZjZVhsY25BNGlwbDlDaEFSUXRqUGNxYWZscWJRTFpRZFgycllkLzhiaG5xaElwQzdTblJsSXhHUHNxdlgifQ==","features":{"auto_web_search":true,"enable_thinking":true,"flags":[],"image_generation":false,"preview_mode":true,"reasoning_effort":"max","vlm_tools_enable":false,"vlm_web_search_enable":false,"vlm_website_mode":false,"web_search":false},"params":{},"extra":{},"mcp_servers":["advanced-search"],"variables":{"{{CURRENT_DATETIME}}":"2026-10-13 09:38:57","{{CURRENT_DATE}}":"2026-10-13","{{CURRENT_TIMEZONE}}":"Africa/Algiers","{{CURRENT_TIME}}":"09:38:57","{{CURRENT_WEEKDAY}}":"Tuesday","{{USER_LANGUAGE}}":"en-US","{{USER_LOCATION}}":"Unknown","{{USER_NAME}}":"vghfroid"},"background_tasks":{"tags_generation":true,"title_generation":true},"id":"d5438f0e-4a84-40dd-af83-20b94cfbd4d1","current_user_message_id":"5cd03db3-4a4a-4b6f-ad5a-0d5a19af52b4","current_user_message_parent_id":null}
