re some of my real data, analyse the data. My knowledge I've got good knowledge about training and how body works biologically (I've also studied things about supplements and gut in that rabbit hole…etc). i stopped training (it's hard to explain) as i didn't really find like something that help me archive my goals, i was motivated like no-one i was almost unstoppable it was like flames burning inside, then slowly it started dying, in my area there's almost zero too none mma or wrestling, even these if they were available doesn't quite target my goal, I've stopped the gym as it wasn't really building what am looking for. I've got a backyard, almost a garden, it got trees and stuff (you can ask if I've got some things, nothing professional tho) but i was honestly just too lazy to do stuff in it such as a pullup bar, i wanted to do also something like hanging a thick metal chain from somewhere high and i could use it to do stuff. I got depressed heavily. Tried to go back trying to re ignite that flame not too long ago about a month or two and failed as i went in deep depression, am still feeling depressed honestly and not into it but it's line am just kicking myself just to write that very message. Also it's not like i lack knowledge but like i found nothing that help me like compile it into something excitable, well that was before at least now i just feel lost and dead.\n\nFirst — you wrote this while feeling dead inside. That's not nothing. Doing the thing with the fire out is literally the core skill of this entire path. Remember what today took, because that's the same muscle everything else runs on.\n\nNow, the analysis you asked for.\n\n## What your data actually says\n\nRead as an athletic profile, you're **a mover with a missing engine.**\n\n- **180cm / 67.3kg** — light frame, high leverage. For your goal this is an *asset*, not something to fix. You don't need mass; you need strength-to-weight and bulletproof connective tissue.\n- **Balance >80s eyes-closed**